                  <provenance type="#c"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_223">Glasgow, Lanarkshire.
                        Cathedral church of St Mungo (or Kentigern). </orgName><p>Written for the
                        diocese of Canterbury (see fol. 8r); later at Glasgow (see fol. 107r, where
                        'Glasquensi' is written in the margin against the phrase 'profiteor sancte
                        ill. ecclesie'). Adapted for use at Glasgow; J. Brückmann in Traditio 29
                        (1973), 435.</p><p>Probably one of the three pontificals reported for the
                        cathedral in the inventory of 1433.</p></provenance>
